A first editable motion version of each reference, fast, to iterate on later against the reference (Scripts/CompareReference.py).
Every measured shot (bible.json) is a scene at its measured length, so the rhythm is the reference's. A shot is a filmed plate by default
(media-text: an excerpt of the reference, replaceable by a render); the recipe below adds what was read on the contact sheets: the words
and their treatment (subtitle, bold caption, giant words, statement), the cards (horizon, charts, dot grid), the retro windows, the
flow diagram, black and white. A recipe entry is (time in the reference, template, params): it applies to the shot playing at that time.
Music: the reference's music reproduced at 99.9 % (bank); effects: the ones isolated from the reference, at their measured times.
FR : une premiere version Motion modifiable de chaque reference, plan par plan, a iterer ensuite contre la reference.
Usage: python3 motion/reproductions/bases.py [slug ...]   (all eleven when no slug)
"""
